the 2006 novel by Daniel Woodrell.

12
01:00:36,000 --> 01:00:42,000
The film stars Jennifer Lawrence as a poverty-stricken teenage girl named Ree Dolly in the rural Ozarks
of Missouri who must locate her missing father to save her family from homelessness.

13
01:05:39,000 --> 01:05:45,000
Winter's Bone received critical acclaim upon release, with high
praise directed towards Lawrence's performance.

14
01:10:42,000 --> 01:10:48,000
The film also emerged as a commercial success at the box-office,
earning $16.1 million on a budget of $2 million.

15
01:15:45,000 --> 01:15:51,000
The film won several awards, including the Grand Jury Prize:
Dramatic Film at the 2010 Sundance Film Festival.

16
01:20:48,000 --> 01:20:54,000
It received four Oscar nominations at the 83rd Academy Awards: Best Picture, Best Adapted Screenplay, Best Actress in a Leading Role for
Lawrence (who at 20 was the second-youngest Best Actress nominee at the time), and Best Supporting Actor for John Hawkes.

17
01:25:51,000 --> 01:25:57,000
In addition, Lawrence was nominated for Best Actress – Motion Picture Drama and Outstanding Leading
Actress at the 68th Golden Globe Awards and 17th Screen Actors Guild Awards, respectively.

